CAT = "cadcCase"; SEG = "CAS"
Q = [
("An agitated client starts shouting in the lobby. The counselor's first step is to:",
 "Speak calmly, give space", ["Block the exit door", "Raise her own voice", "Hold his arm firmly"],
 "De-escalation starts with a calm voice, a non-threatening stance and enough physical space, which lowers the sense of threat for everyone."),
("Which number connects a person to the national Suicide and Crisis Lifeline?",
 "988", ["311", "411", "611"],
 "The 988 Suicide and Crisis Lifeline offers call, text and chat support. In an immediate medical emergency, call 911."),
("A client collapses with slow breathing and blue lips after using in the restroom. After calling 911, staff should:",
 "Give naloxone", ["Offer black coffee", "Let him sleep", "Give him water"],
 "These are signs of opioid overdose. The FDA notes naloxone can be given by people without medical training, and it reverses the overdose while help arrives."),
("Linking a client to housing, benefits and medical care is the core of:",
 "Case management", ["Psychotherapy", "Group process", "Utilization review"],
 "Case management connects clients with the services they need beyond counseling and coordinates those services."),
("After referring a client to a dental clinic, the counselor should:",
 "Follow up on it", ["Close the case", "Leave it to the client", "Call the clinic daily"],
 "Follow-up checks that the client reached the service and that the referral met the need, which is part of good case management."),
("A pregnant client with opioid use disorder wants to stop methadone today. The counselor should:",
 "Urge her to see her prescriber", ["Support stopping today", "Tell her to halve the dose", "Wait until after she gives birth"],
 "SAMHSA notes that MOUD improves birth outcomes and that patients should consult their doctor before stopping. Dose changes are a medical decision."),
("Treatment for adolescents tends to work best when it:",
 "Involves the family", ["Excludes the family", "Copies adult programs", "Relies on scare tactics"],
 "Family involvement is a strong part of effective adolescent treatment, since family rules, supervision and conflict affect a teen's use."),
("A transgender client is repeatedly called by the wrong name by staff. The best response affirms her by:",
 "Using her chosen name", ["Using her legal name", "Avoiding the topic", "Referring her to a specialist"],
 "Using a client's chosen name and pronouns shows respect, builds trust and keeps an LGBTQ+ client engaged in care."),
("A drug court client says treatment is just more punishment. The counselor should:",
 "Clarify roles and build trust", ["Promise no reports to court", "Act like a probation officer", "Refuse the referral"],
 "With a justice-involved client, the counselor explains what will and will not be reported under the signed consent and focuses on the client's own goals."),
("A client in medication treatment sees a prescriber, a nurse and a counselor. With proper consent, the team should:",
 "Share one coordinated plan", ["Set separate goals each", "Avoid talking together", "Let the insurer decide care"],
 "Collaboration across disciplines, with the client's consent, keeps care consistent and avoids conflicting advice."),
("Family members who call in sick for a client's hangovers and pay off his drug debts are often described as:",
 "Enabling", ["Detaching", "Intervening", "Reframing"],
 "Enabling shields a person from the consequences of use, which can make change less likely. Family work helps relatives set limits with support."),
("Which practice best protects a counselor from the effects of hearing clients' trauma stories?",
 "Supervision and self-care", ["Taking on more clients", "Avoiding trauma topics", "Working longer hours"],
 "Regular supervision, peer support and self-care help counselors manage the emotional load of trauma work. Avoiding trauma topics fails clients."),
("A trauma-informed program puts priority on clients' physical and emotional:",
 "Safety", ["Compliance", "Obedience", "Productivity"],
 "Safety is one of the six guiding principles of a trauma-informed approach that SAMHSA publishes, along with peer support. Clients who feel unsafe cannot engage in treatment."),
("A client says her partner hits her when he drinks. The counselor's first priority is:",
 "Planning for her safety", ["Starting couples counseling", "Telling her to leave today", "Confronting the partner"],
 "With domestic violence, safety planning comes first. Couples counseling can raise the danger, and the client decides when and whether to leave."),
("To help a client find licensed treatment programs nearby, the counselor can point her to:",
 "FindTreatment.gov", ["Medicare.gov", "USA.gov", "StudentAid.gov"],
 "FindTreatment.gov is SAMHSA's locator for state-licensed substance use and mental health treatment facilities."),
("A client keeps missing sessions because she has no ride. The counselor should:",
 "Explore transportation help", ["Discharge her for absences", "Lecture her on commitment", "Wait for her to call"],
 "Identifying resources that remove a practical barrier, such as transit passes or rides, keeps a willing client in care."),
]
